UID:1bffd2bb8d4759b0aa0b3c32d9b061b2@littlejumbobar.com
DESCRIPTION:Sometimes the most powerful revivals happen when five master m
 usicians gather in an intimate room and decide to resurrect the soul that 
 made jazz matter in the first place. Jacob Rodriguez's world-traveling bar
 itone sax brings the grit of San Antonio streets and the polish of Grammy 
 stages\, ready to channel stories through reed and breath that connect Bro
 oklyn underground scenes to Blue Ridge mountaintops. Quinn Sternberg ancho
 rs this sonic revival with bass lines that don't just walk—they preach\,
  transforming rhythm section duties into gravitational sermons that make e
 veryone else sound sanctified.\n\nJoe Enright treats his drum kit like a r
 evival tent\, his sticks weaving rhythmic narratives that bridge Asheville
 's mountain soul with metropolitan jazz sophistication\, while Alex Taub's
  ...
LOCATION:Little Jumbo: 241 Broadway St.\, Asheville\, NC 28801
URL:https://www.littlejumbobar.com/events/1809/soul-jazz-revival
